+Tailored Runbook — ScoutAV (example vehicle)
+
+Purpose
+- This runbook provides exact commands, environment variables and acceptance criteria required to move the Aegis scaffold to a validated evidence state for the ScoutAV vehicle class (wheeled urban vehicle). Adapt hostnames, interfaces and thresholds to your hardware.
+
+Assumptions / variables to set
+- Representative ECU/controller hostnames: SCOUT_ECU1, SCOUT_ECU2 (SSH reachable from operator runner).
+- CAN interfaces on ECUs: can0 (or can1). TSN interfaces: eth1 (if present).
+- Self-hosted runners: one builder (label: aegis/role=builder), one hardware runner (label: aegis/role=hardware).
+- Secrets (in environment or GitHub secrets):
+  - COSIGN_KMS_URI  (e.g., kms://projects/.../keys/cosign)
+  - REKOR_SERVER
+  - WATTTIME_API_KEY
+  - S3_UPLOAD (evidence bucket, e.g., s3://aegis-evidence/scoutav/<run-id>/)
+  - NPU_RUNNERS (comma-separated hostnames for NPU smoke test)
+
+Operator preparatory steps
+1) Verify runner hardening and tools (on each labeled runner):
+   sudo /bin/bash ops/infra/hardening/check_runner_hardening.sh
+   - Expected: exits 0. If missing commands, run provision_and_label_runners.sh and install vendor SDKs.
+
+2) Ensure golden traces are present:
+   sudo mkdir -p /opt/aegis
+   sudo cp <your_golden_trace.ndjson> /opt/aegis/golden_trace.ndjson
+
+Hardware & RT validation (produce signed rt_slo_proof)
+1) Create target list file (ops/av/rt/rt_sweep_targets.json), example:
+   [
+     {"host": "SCOUT_ECU1", "iface": "can0"},
+     {"host": "SCOUT_ECU2", "iface": "can0"}
+   ]
+
+2) Run sweep (example):
+   COSIGN_KMS_URI=$COSIGN_KMS_URI S3_UPLOAD=$S3_UPLOAD TARGETS="SCOUT_ECU1:can0,SCOUT_ECU2:can0" \
+     ./ops/validation/run_rt_sweep_and_sign.sh /tmp/scoutav_rt_proofs
+
+3) Inspect proofs:
+   jq . /tmp/scoutav_rt_proofs/*/rt_slo_proof.json
+   - Acceptance criteria for ScoutAV (example):
+     - p99 loop jitter <= 0.5 ms  (set per controller; adjust based on vehicle dynamics)
+     - safe_stop_ms <= computed threshold from ops/av/slo/vehicle_slo_table.py (run with vehicle params)
+
+4) If SLOs fail:
+   - Run remediation helper:
+     python3 ops/validation/rt_remediation_agent.py --report /tmp/scoutav_rt_proofs/<target>/rt_slo_proof.json --out /tmp/scoutav_rt_proofs/<target>/remediation.json
+   - Follow remediation suggestions (CPU isolation, IRQ affinity, chrt settings). Re-run sweep.
+
+HIL campaigns & formal closure (controller certification)
+1) Prepare scenarios file (one command per line): ops/av/certification/scout_scenarios.txt
+   Example lines:
+     ./ops/av/certification/scripts/run_brake_emergency.sh --host SCOUT_ECU1
+     ./ops/av/certification/scripts/run_steer_recovery.sh --host SCOUT_ECU1
+
+2) Run exhaustive HIL + formal loop:
+   COSIGN_KMS_URI=$COSIGN_KMS_URI ./ops/robotics/control/certified/run_exhaustive_hil_and_close_formal.sh \
+     --scenarios-file ops/av/certification/scout_scenarios.txt --golden /opt/aegis/golden_trace.ndjson --out /tmp/scout_hil_cert --cosign $COSIGN_KMS_URI --max-iter 5
+
+3) Acceptance criteria:
+   - HIL: campaign_summary.json shows zero critical scenario failures (compare_ok==true, ran_ok==true for all critical scenarios).
+   - Formal: Apalache reports no unresolved counterexamples for safety invariants in TLA+ specs targeted at the controller.
+   - Produce signed HIL cert bundle and upload to S3 for audit.
+
+Perception long-tail & NPU validation (sim -> HIL -> field)
+1) Generate and run sim packs:
+   ./ops/av/perception/scale/run_sim_hil_field_pipeline.sh --packs 20 --per-pack 200 --parallel 6 --out /tmp/scout_perception_pipeline --npu-runners "$NPU_RUNNERS" --cosign "$COSIGN_KMS_URI"
+
+2) Collect adversarial dataset and retrain:
+   - Collected at /tmp/scout_perception_pipeline/adv_dataset/adv_data.ndjson
+   - Trigger retrain (auto_retrain_pipeline invoked by pipeline); validate output ONNX models were signed and tested on NPU runners.
+
+3) Acceptance criteria:
+   - Obstacle detection FN rate <= 1e-3 in certified envelope (verify via ops/agents/safety evaluation scripts).
+   - ONNX runtime smoke tests pass on all NPU runners listed in NPU_RUNNERS (ensure auto_retrain_pipeline produced signed artifacts).
+
+Supply-chain & CI gates (staging -> production)
+1) Ensure builders are hardened and labeled (run on each builder):
+   sudo ./ops/infra/hardening/provision_and_label_runners.sh LABELS="role=builder,npu=true"
+   Verify: /etc/aegis-runner-labels contains the label and check_runner_hardening.sh passes.
+
+2) Push changes to staging branch and let CI run the provenance gate. For manual testing run locally:
+   IMAGE_MANIFESTS=deploy.yaml REKOR_SERVER=$REKOR_SERVER python3 ops/ci/promotion_gate/enforce_builder_provenance.py
+   - Acceptance: enforcement script exits 0 only if all images are cosign-signed and Rekor entries are present.
+
+Carbon gate & override policy
+1) Run monitoring (14 days recommended) on the chosen region:
+   python3 ops/carbon/monitor_tune.py --duration-s 1209600 --interval-s 300 --region US-CA --out /tmp/carbon_tune_scoutav.json
+2) Tune threshold to keep FP < 5%. When enforcing, use override artifacts as needed:
+   python3 ops/carbon/override_signer.py --approval-id SCOUT-OVR-001 --approved-by owner@example.com --scope '{"manifests":"deploy.yaml"}' --out /tmp/override.json
+   cosign verify /tmp/override.json
+
+Submission to certifier and closing findings
+1) Build final safety case & cert bundle:
+   python3 ops/certifier/auditor_package_builder.py --artifacts-root . --out /tmp/scoutav_cert_bundle.tar.gz --cosign-key "$COSIGN_KMS_URI" --s3 "$S3_UPLOAD" --vehicle ScoutAV
+2) Submit and track findings:
+   python3 ops/certifier/submit_and_track_findings.py --bundle /tmp/scoutav_cert_bundle.tar.gz --upload-url https://certifier.example/upload --findings-url https://certifier.example/findings --api-token "$CERTIFIER_API_TOKEN" --outdir /tmp/certifier_findings
+3) Acceptance:
+   - Certifier returns either "accepted" or a set of findings with remediation timeline; all critical findings closed and evidence re-submitted.
+
+Operator escalation
+- If any HIL/apalache or RT SLO failures occur, notify Controls Lead and Safety Officer and attach the signed bundle path and remediation.json from the failed run.
+
+Notes
+- Update thresholds and scenario lists to match ScoutAV dynamics and safety envelope before running.
+- Replace placeholder scenario runners with real HIL rig commands appropriate to your setup.
+
